<title>THAILAND: Finance One denies notes default rumour.</title>
<headline>Finance One denies notes default rumour.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's leading finance company denied rumours in the stock market on Wednesday that the firm would not be able to meet payments on its promissory notes worth $66 million.</p>
<p>&quot;I have talked to the funding department and these rumours are absolutely not true. We will meet the payments,&quot; a Finance One vice-president Vichara Na Ranong told Reuters.</p>
<p>The rumours sent Finance One stocks down the daily limit to 37 baht, off four baht by the close.</p>
</text>
